{
  "description": "The proposal seeks the refurbishment and partial redevelopment of an existing single-storey building on a narrow plot measuring approximately 2.15m wide by 16m long. The building comprises an occupied front storage unit, which will be retained in employment/storage use, and a rear section that has remained vacant for approximately four years.\n\nThe vacant rear section will be partially demolished and shortened to accommodate a ground-floor kitchen, bathroom and staircase, together with an enlarged private rear garden of approximately 5.7m².\n\nThe building will be extended upwards to create a two-storey, one-bedroom dwelling with a gable roof. The upper floor will provide bedroom and living accommodation, including a double-height living space and mezzanine suitable for home-office or study. The building will be finished in yellow brick to provide a simple and cohesive appearance.\n\nThe revised scheme responds to Croydon Council’s pre-application advice under Ref. 22/03654/PRE dated 1 February 2023, particularly the concerns regarding residential quality, narrowness, amenity space and outlook. The proposal provides substantially improved accommodation while making efficient use of the constrained site.\n\nThe proposal increases the GIA from approximately 31.18m² to 72.54m², providing generous internal floorspace for a one-bedroom dwelling. Approximately 10.75m² of the proposed floorspace will be retained in non-residential/employment use..\n\nThe retention of the occupied front storage unit ensures that the proposal does not result in the complete loss of the existing employment function. Instead, residential use is primarily introduced within the long-term vacant rear section, bringing this underused part of the site back into productive use. This area has been vacant for more than 18 months.\n\nOverall, the proposal provides an improved one-bedroom dwelling, retains employment/storage space, provides private outdoor amenity space and makes efficient use of previously developed land while responding to the Council’s previous pre-application advice.",
